topics.detail:
AI Overuse argues that AI is used for ads or clout. AI is used excessively in software engineering. Managers and underlings rely on AI for summaries and writing. AI is used for simple tasks that require little effort. AI Art argues that AI output is not creative. AI generated content is slop.

@deathbymeteor.bsky.social: “Lol, imagine saying "I used multiple AI's to do a job that the person I'm arguing with does on their own routinely" as a way of strengthening your argument. Your chatbot was wrong, you should feel bad relying on it”

AI Overuse (86.7%) says AI is overused for trivial tasks. AI Art (13.3%) says AI generated art is not real art.

Politics.detail:
Protest Effectiveness argues that Violent protests are more effective. Peaceful protests are effective for organizing voters. French Protests argues that Protests in France are a deeply ingrained cultural response. The French protests are justified despite violent outbursts. Protests in France are being met with brutal police repression.

@sharonk.bsky.social: “vibe on /r/France during the protests is that everyone is more or less on board with the social movement but fear that the images of property damage are going to boost Le Pen”

Protest Effectiveness (51.3%) says Protests are effective ways to organize voters. French Protests (48.7%) says Protests are happening in France.

